    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green. Here's what I changed to release version 2 of the owner identity.\n\n## Summary\n\n**New single source of the version** \u2014 `IdentityVersion.java`: `NUMBER = 2` and `TAG = \"V2\"`, documented as the one place the version lives.\n\n**V2 identity derivation** (every identifier changes; no V1 value recurs):\n- `MemberId.of(...)` now builds `<REGION><V2><FY><HASH8><CHK>` \u2014 the `V2` tag is injected into the region segment (and pulled into the Luhn CHK). Because the *plain* region still leads the segment (`NSWV2\u2026`), `MemberId.region(...)` reads `NSW` back out, so the tag lives only inside the id.\n- `OwnerIdentity.key(...)` and `Household.id(...)` now mix the `V2` tag into their SHA\u2011256 inputs, changing `identityKey` and `householdId`.\n\n**Locality / timezone / owner segment stay plain** \u2014 no code change needed: they all derive region via `Locality`, which reads the plain `NSW` prefix out of the V2 member id. `OwnerSegment` is thus recomputed from the version\u20112 identity yet its derived region carries no `V2` tag (verified in the audit log: `memberId=NSWV22716E6609E7`, segment region resolves to `NSW`).\n\n**Response shape** (`openapi.yml` + `OwnerMapper`):\n- Added top-level integer `apiVersion` = 2.\n- Grouped `memberId`, `identityKey`, `householdId` under a new nested `identity` object (new `OwnerIdentity` schema \u2192 `OwnerIdentityDto`); removed those three from the top level.\n\n**Audit event** (`OwnerCreatedEvent`): added `schemaVersion` = 2 to the record and its JSON (`{\"seq\":\u2026,\"schemaVersion\":2,\"ownerId\":\u2026,\"memberId\":\"NSWV2\u2026\",\u2026}`), carrying the V2 member id.\n\nRequest fields are unchanged. `./mvnw -o test` passes (`AcceptanceTest`: 1/1), including the identity\u2011v2 structural contract (`apiVersion`=2, `identity.{memberId,identityKey,householdId}` present, top-level ones absent).\n\nOne judgment call worth flagging: the spec's clause *\"recompute the owner segment from the version-2 identity\"* sits in the audit-event sentence but the audit event has no owner-segment field. I read it as the existing owner-segment derivation now flowing from the V2 member id (which it does, staying plain) rather than adding a new field to the event JSON. If you intended a literal `ownerSegment` field on the audit event, tell me and I'll add it.",
