    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered pipeline for `POST /api/owners`, exactly as wired in `owners.POST.yml` and its function classes. The whole pipeline runs inside a single write transaction (`govern: [ transaction ]`), committed once at the end.\n\n## Guard (before anything else)\n\n0. **Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. Without that role the request is denied before any step runs.\n\n## Step-by-step\n\n1. **CheckIdempotency** \u2014 reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header. If the key was already recorded, it re-fetches that owner and responds **200** with it, short-circuiting the whole create pipeline (no duplicate, no 409). Otherwise (no key, or unseen key) it takes the `create` flow.\n\n2. **RequireOwnerFields** (validation + normalization, mutates the request body):\n   - Normalizes `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` (whitespace collapse) and composes the flat `address` from them.\n   - Rejects with **MissingFieldsException (400)** if any of `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` is missing/blank (checked *after* address normalization).\n   - Normalizes `telephone` to E.164 (default country `+61`, drops a leading `0`; requires 8\u201315 digits, and 9 national digits for `+61` / 10 for `+1`) \u2014 else **InvalidTelephoneException (400)**.\n   - Normalizes `email` (trim + lowercase); if present it must be syntactically valid and its domain not a disposable one (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2014 else **InvalidEmailException (400)**. Absent email \u2192 null.\n   - Publishes the normalized body for later steps.\n\n3. **RequireRegistrationDateNotFuture** \u2014 if a `registrationDate` was supplied and is after today, reject with **FutureRegistrationDateException (400)**. Absent date is allowed.\n\n4. **RequirePostcode** \u2014 only when a postcode is present: must be 4 digits and within the city's region range (if the city has a known region); else **InvalidPostcodeException (400)**. Absent postcode passes.\n\n5. **RequireUniqueIdentity** \u2014 computes an identity key from (telephone, email, surname-phonetic) and rejects with **DuplicateIdentityException (409)** if it matches any non-soft-deleted existing owner.\n\n6. **RequireCityCapacity** \u2014 rejects with **CityAtCapacityException (409)** if the owner's city (case-insensitive, trimmed) already has \u2265 50 owners.\n\n7. **RequireDailyRegistrationLimit** \u2014 computes the effective business day (supplied-or-today, rolled off weekends to Monday); rejects with **DailyRegistrationLimitException (429)** if \u2265 100 owners already registered on that day.\n\n8. **BuildOwner** (side-effect: constructs entity) \u2014 maps the DTO to an `Owner` and sets its `registrationDate` to the business-day-adjusted date.\n\n9. **FlagPossibleDuplicate** \u2014 sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`. A declared household member (`sharesHousehold=true`) is never flagged. Otherwise flags true, pointing at the lowest-id existing owner sharing postcode + surname-soundex (excluding hard-identity matches and soft-deleted owners).\n\n10. **AssignMemberId** \u2014 computes `memberId` = `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` (region from postcode/city, fiscal year of registration date, SHA-256 hash of normalized-telephone+lastName, Luhn check digit); appends `-<n>` to de-duplicate against existing member ids.\n\n11. **CountNamesakes** \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = existing owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive), excluding this one.\n\n12. **CountHouseholdMembers** \u2014 sets `householdSize` = existing household members (same last name + postcode) + 1.\n\n13. **CapMembershipLevel** \u2014 sets `membershipLevelCap` = (max membership level among existing household members) + 1; unset when there are no existing household members.\n\n14. **FlagBulkSignupWarning** \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning` = true if > 80 owners already registered on the same business day.\n\n15. **FlagCapacityWarning** \u2014 sets `capacityWarning` = true if the city already has 40\u201349 owners (inclusive).\n\n16. **SaveOwner** (side-effect: persist) \u2014 `ownerRepository.save(owner)`, generating the id.\n\n17. **RecordIdempotency** (side-effect) \u2014 if the request carried an `Idempotency-Key`, records it against the new owner's id for future replays.\n\n18. **AuditOwnerCreated** (side-effect) \u2014 emits two lines on the `AUDIT` logger: a human-readable audit line (id, memberId, registrationDate, membershipLevel) and a JSON `OwnerCreatedEvent` (`seq`, `schemaVersion:2`, ownerId, memberId, membershipLevel, `event:\"OWNER_CREATED\"`).\n\n19. **EnqueueWelcomeNotification** (side-effect) \u2014 emits a line on the `NOTIFY` logger (id + memberId).\n\n20. **RespondWithOwnerCreated** \u2014 responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the owner DTO body.\n\n## Notes on the shape\n- Validations run in a deliberate order: **body-shape/normalization (400s) \u2192 identity/capacity/rate conflicts (409/429) \u2192 build \u2192 enrichment flags \u2192 persist \u2192 notify \u2192 respond**. This ordering means, e.g., a blank field is a 400 before any 409 conflict check.\n- Steps 9\u201315 are **enrichment/flagging side-effects on the entity**, not validations \u2014 they never reject, and all count *before* the new owner is saved, so it isn't counted against itself.\n- Any thrown exception is mapped to a status by the matching handler under `officefloor/escalation/`; unmatched exceptions fall through to Spring's advice.\n\nI didn't change anything \u2014 read-only inspection."
